  "title": "stcommunity.st.com may need update/redirection",
  "content": "<p>I have some stored links, which use the stcommunity.st.com third-level domain (note that it is not community but <strong>st</strong>community), for example <a href=\"https://stcommunity.st.com/t5/stm32-mcus/empty-check-mechanism-on-stm32/ta-p/49369\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow ugc\" target=\"_blank\">https://stcommunity.st.com/t5/stm32-mcus/empty-check-mechanism-on-stm32/ta-p/49369</a></p><p>These now display a message saying Khoros is down. As it’s an st.com domain, i.e. under ST’s control, these may be changed.</p><p>A proper redirection would be nice.</p><p>JW</p><p> </p><figure><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://uploads-eu-west-1.insided.com/stmicroelectronics-en/attachment/ab9d2604-cc73-4129-8c3b-0ff1f0a69f3a.png\" /></figure><p> </p>",
